-- title:
--   Theorem 6.2 — non-i.i.d. state tomography with round complexity $O(sn^2\epsilon^{-4}\delta^{-2})$
-- statement:
--   There is a constant $C$ such that for every source model there is a single tomography learner $L$ (Definition 6.1) with the following property. For all $n,s,t\in\mathbb N$, all $\epsilon=1/a$ and $\delta=1/b$ with $a,b\in\mathbb N_{\ge1}$, every $m\ge1$ with
--   $$m\ \ge\ C\cdot\frac{s\,n^2}{\epsilon^4\delta^2},$$
--   and every source $\rho_{R_1\dots R_m}$ generated by a program of length at most $s$,
--   $$\Pr\Big[\mathrm{TD}(\sigma,\rho_{R_i|h})\le\epsilon:\ i\leftarrow[m],\ (h,\sigma)\leftarrow L(\mathsf{param},\rho_{R_1\dots R_{i-1}})\Big]\ \ge\ 1-\delta .$$
--
--   The learner chooses its own measurement on the past registers and outputs a full classical description of the conditional state of the next register; unlike i.i.d. tomography, the registers may be arbitrarily correlated, and the number of rounds depends on the source only through the length $s$ of its shortest generating program.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: the paper's source model (its fixed gate set, machine model and encoding) → every SourceModel gen (published with the base mission); the learner may depend on gen, the constant C may not; reason: the proof uses only that the class {gen n t T : |T| ≤ s} has fewer than 2^{s+1} members; the statement specializes to the paper's model
--   - encoding: measurement procedure on (R1, …, R_{i−1}) inducing a POVM M = {E_x} that depends only on param and i; output h = (M, x) and σ determined by param, i, x → TomoLearner: for each (s, t, n, a, b, i−1) a finite POVM (PSD effects summing to 1) and a density operator for each record; reason: Definition 6.1 items 2–3; a learner of this type is a learner in the paper's sense, so the existence claim is not weakened
--   - encoding: round complexity O(s n² ε⁻⁴ δ⁻²) → C · s · n² · a⁴ · b² ≤ m with one C uniform in n, s, t, a, b, the source model and the source; 1 ≤ m; reason: the proof gives m ≥ 4(2+√2)²(n+1)²(s+1)ε⁻⁴δ⁻² (Eq. (183)); the cases n = 0 and s = 0 are trivially solvable; i ← [m] needs m ≥ 1
--   - encoding: ε⁻¹, δ⁻¹ ∈ ℕ, TD(ρ, σ) = ½‖ρ − σ‖₁ → ε = 1/a, δ = 1/b with a, b ≥ 1; ½ · WildeQIT.traceDist; reason: Lean convention; same instances
-- source:
--   Hiroka, Hsieh, Shirakawa, Universal Inductive Inference of Quantum States, arXiv:2609.36912 (PDF of 2026-11-02, sha256 ac6387756651cc50c671f36acf1ef987db0df0c463581cd948250204441f6925), §6, Theorem 6.2, Eq. (124), p.29 (= Theorem 1.2, p.6), proof pp.30–35 (Eq. (183)); Definition 6.1, p.29

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_QIndInf_Supplement_TomoLearner

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace QIndInf.Supplement

open QIndInf

/-- **Theorem 6.2 (non-i.i.d. state tomography with round complexity `O(s n² ε⁻⁴ δ⁻²)`).** There
is a constant `C` such that for every source model there is a single tomography learner `L`
(Definition 6.1) with the following property. For all register sizes `n`, program-length bounds
`s`, time bounds `t`, accuracies `ε = 1/a` and confidences `δ = 1/b` (`a, b ≥ 1`), every number of
rounds `m ≥ 1` with `m ≥ C · s · n² · ε⁻⁴ · δ⁻²` and every source generated by a program of length at
most `s`,
`Pr[TD(σ, ρ_{R_i|h}) ≤ ε : i ← [m], (h, σ) ← L(param, ρ_{R₁…R_{i−1}})] ≥ 1 − δ`.

arXiv:2609.36912 (PDF of 2026-11-02), §6, Theorem 6.2, Eq. (124), p.29 (= Theorem 1.2, p.6), with
Definition 6.1, Eqs. (121)–(123), p.29; the proof gives `m ≥ 4(2+√2)²(n+1)²(s+1)ε⁻⁴δ⁻²`
(Eq. (183), p.35).

**Formalization Note.**
* The source class `C_{n,m}[s,t]` (Eq. (121)) is `{(gen n t T).state m : |T| ≤ s}` for the paper's
  source model; the statement holds for every source model (`SourceModel`, published with the base
  mission). The learner may depend on the model, the constant `C` may not.
* `O(s n² ε⁻⁴ δ⁻²)` is `r(n, s, a, b) = C · s · n² · a⁴ · b²`, one constant uniform in `t`, the
  source model and the source.
* `m ≥ 1` because `i` is drawn uniformly from `[m]`. -/
theorem theorem_6_2 :
    ∃ C : ℕ, ∀ gen : SourceModel, ∃ L : TomoLearner,
      ∀ (n s t a b m : ℕ), 1 ≤ a → 1 ≤ b → 1 ≤ m → C * s * n ^ 2 * a ^ 4 * b ^ 2 ≤ m →
        ∀ T : List Bool, T.length ≤ s →
          1 - 1 / (b : ℝ) ≤ tomoSuccessProb L s t a b (gen n t T) m := by sorry

end QIndInf.Supplement
